### 2.1 Garbled Lafont Active Pairs (Yao / AIK Randomized Encodings)
Every interaction-net wire carries a masked bit $w_i = b_i \oplus k_i$ under a fresh wire mask $k_i$. An active-pair NAND2 reduction evaluates directly on masked wires via `ci-garbled-nand`.
- **Formal Certificate (`ci-thm-garbled-inet-correct`):** For *all* masks $(k_a, k_b, k_o) \in \mathbb{B}^3$ and *all* inputs $(a, b) \in \mathbb{B}^2$,
  $$k_o \oplus \mathrm{GarbledNAND}(k_a, k_b, k_o, k_a \oplus a, k_b \oplus b) \equiv \mathrm{NAND}(a, b).$$
Because every interaction-net rule is strictly local (degree-2 active pair) and confluent, masking composes across arbitrary interaction graphs with zero global coordination.

